nded` predicate, add a fact `suspended(gamma)`, and update the rule `r1` to include a `not suspended(?task)` term.\n\nLet's construct the JSON carefully following the exact schema structure from the examples.\nDomains: task (symbol), hours (int), priority (int).\nEntities: alpha, beta, gamma in task domain.\nPredicates: effort(task, hours), priority(task, priority), blocked(task), selectable(task), suspended(task).\nFacts: effort and priority facts as before. blocked(gamma) as before. suspended(gamma) as new fact.\nRules: r1 with body checking effort <= 2, priority >= 2, not blocked, not suspended.\nQuery: select ?task where selectable(?task).\n\nLet's verify the structure matches exactly.\nKeys: schema_version, domains, entities, predicates, facts, rules, query. (Order in JSON doesn't strictly matter but I'll follow semantic order as requested or just standard JSON object).\nThe prompt says: \"Fill the object in this semantic order: - name finite domains and entities - declare schema and predicate signatures - write observed facts with truth values - encode explicit not terms or false facts - write implication rules - write the query goal\"\n\nI will construct the JSON carefully.\n\nDomains:\n[{\"id\":\"task\",\"type\":\"symbol\",\"values\":[\"alpha\",\"beta\",\"gamma\"]},{\"id\":\"hours\",\"type\":\"int\",\"values\":[1,2,3]},{\"id\":\"priority\",\"type\":\"int\",\"values\":[1,2,3]}]\n\nEntities:\n[{\"domain\":\"task\",\"id\":\"alpha\"},{\"domain\":\"task\",\"id\":\"beta\"},{\"domain\":\"task\",\"id\":\"gamma\"}]\n\nPredicates:\n[{\"arg_types\":[\"task\",\"hours\"],\"id\":\"effort\"},{\"arg_types\":[\"task\",\"priority\"],\"id\":\"priority\"},{\"arg_types\":[\"task\"],\"id\":\"blocked\"},{\"arg_types\":[\"task\"],\"id\":\"suspended\"},{\"arg_types\":[\"task\"],\"id\":\"selectable\"}]\n\nFacts:\n[{\"args\":[\"alpha\",1],\"predicate\":\"effort\",\"truth\":true},{\"args\":[\"beta\",3],\"predicate\":\"effort\",\"truth\":true},{\"","usage":{"completion_tokens":640,"prom